# Reuse existing dev servers

Do not start `npm run dev` or `npm run dev:admin` on your own.

1. Check whether **5173** is already listening (user terminal or a prior session).
2. If it is, use `http://localhost:5173`. Do not start a second instance. Do not kill it.
3. Start the server only when verification needs a live app **and** the port is free.

```powershell
Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 5173 -State Listen -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
```

```text
❌ BAD — npm run dev:admin without checking; then kill the user's server
✅ GOOD — detect the listener, then open that URL
```

From the repo root the script is `npm run dev:admin`. Inside `admin/` it is `npm run dev`. Vite will not move off 5173.

Stop only servers you started in this chat. See `close-terminals-after-work`.
